From 8e62b00eeb1976b33971f6c5b4938015e228a28f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuanyuan Chen <cyyever@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:05:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] hipGraph: reuse kernel-argument slots across exec updates

Every hipGraphExecUpdate / hipGraphExec*SetParams re-captures the node's
packet and bump-allocates a fresh kernel-argument slot; nothing is
reclaimed until the exec is destroyed. An exec updated once per launch
(per generated token in LLM serving) therefore grows device memory
without bound and eventually exhausts it (#10713, the trigger for
#10021).

Track the slots each node's packets use. When an update commits, the
node's previous slots are retired; they become reusable once no launch
that may still read them is in flight (the in-flight count, bracketed
by Run and the launch-completion callback, has dropped to zero since).
A failed capture or update discards the new slots and keeps the old
ones. Free slots are kept in a (device, size)-ordered multimap for
best-fit reuse.

Closes #10713

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
